<BaseLayout site="main" title="Contact — jsonversal" description="How to contact the operator of jsonversal, report a wrong result or request a data correction. Includes the current status of our email address." canonical="https://jsonversal.com/contact/">
  <h1>Contact</h1>
  <p class="text-muted">Last updated: 2026-11-08</p>

  <p><strong>Operator:</strong> Jim (Maoming, Guangdong, China) ·
  <a href="https://github.com/eyetoolkit" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">eyetoolkit on GitHub</a>.
  Background and responsibilities are on the <a href="/about/">About page</a>.</p>

  <h2>Primary channel — the public issue tracker</h2>
  <p>The channel that currently works is our GitHub issue tracker:</p>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/eyetoolkit/jsonversal-monorepo/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><strong>Open an issue at github.com/eyetoolkit/jsonversal-monorepo/issues</strong></a></p>
  <p>Use it for wrong tool results, bug reports, data corrections, privacy and data-rights requests, licensing
  questions, and anything an auditor or advertiser needs from the operator. The tracker is public: you can read
  it without an account, and posting requires only a free GitHub account. Replies are posted in the same thread,
  so the answer stays verifiable.</p>

  <h2>Email status — please read before writing</h2>
  <p><code>hello@jsonversal.com</code> <strong>cannot currently receive mail</strong>. The jsonversal.com domain
  has no MX records and email routing is disabled, so messages sent to that address are not delivered. Older
  versions of our legal pages listed it; those pages now point here instead.</p>
  <p>Please <strong>do not</strong> send mail to that address — use the issue tracker above. We will publish a
  working address on this page as soon as mail delivery is configured, and update this notice at the same time.
  We would rather say so plainly than leave an address on the site that silently drops your message.</p>

  <h2>What to include</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The URL of the page or tool, and the input that produced the problem (please redact secrets — the tracker is public).</li>
    <li>What you expected and what you got; a browser and version if it looks rendering-related.</li>
    <li>For privacy or data-rights requests, say which region's rules apply so we can route it correctly.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Other sites in the versal family</h2>
  <p>The same operator runs <a href="https://mquickcalc.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">mQuickCalc</a>
  (everyday converters), <a href="https://finance.mquickcalc.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">mQuickCalc Finance</a>,
  <a href="https://health.mquickcalc.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Health</a> and
  <a href="https://cover.mquickcalc.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Cover</a>. For those sites,
  the same issue tracker is the fastest route.</p>
</BaseLayout>
